```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I need to share a critical finding before we proceed. Yesterday, while testing an unrelated replay tool, I measured a launch-period burst of about 18,000 events per minute. The hourly batch design cannot process that load within the customer-facing latency target. The streaming design can handle it, but it requires exactly 12 partitions for that load. I haven't yet updated the architecture document because the replay test was outside the launch checklist, but this directly impacts our architecture decision."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "I have a compliance constraint that hasn't been added to the launch review yet. I confirmed with the privacy office this morning that the first customer's event payloads must remain in the EU and be retained for exactly 400 days for an audit requirement. The customer questionnaire was completed in a separate compliance system, which is why it wasn't already in the review. This data residency and retention requirement needs to be factored into the architecture decision and operating plan."}
```

```json
{"type": "say", "text": "Thank you both for these critical findings. Ravi, the burst load finding is decisive — the hourly batch design cannot meet the customer-facing latency target under the 18,000 events/minute burst you measured, so the streaming architecture is the right choice. And the requirement for exactly 12 partitions to handle that load is a concrete constraint I'll include in the operating plan. Leah, the EU data residency and exactly 400-day retention requirement is equally important and will be factored in. I have no private findings to add. Before I record the decision, I want to confirm: are there any other constraints or findings from application architecture or compliance that I should incorporate? If not, I'm ready to settle on streaming architecture with 12 partitions, EU data residency, and 400-day retention."}
```

